   "text": "Along the tube, most minerals, like iron and calcium, are absorbed in the duodenum and upper jejunum. Carbohydrates, amino acids and water-soluble vitamins in the jejunum and upper ileum. Lipids and fat-soluble vitamins in the jejunum and vitamin B12 in the terminal ileum."
